" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165470 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186516296 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165470 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186516388 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165470 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186516471 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165470 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186516524 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165470 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186516585 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165470 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165470 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165470 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186516388 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165470 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "69f902f3-a692-59e5-9182-a1ffd7507170" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166592 #edb/ref 1069 "e-8337" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166592 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nIf $y = 2\\arsinh{x^2},$ then find $\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166592 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "181b2a5e-7caf-5527-8602-e67a945affde" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166592 #edb/ref 1074 "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic sine function is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\arsinh x) = \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{x^2+1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{({x}^{2})}^{2}+1}}\\cdot {({x}^{2})}^{′} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{4}+1}}\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =\\frac{4x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{4}+1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166593 #edb/ref 1069 "e-8338" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166593 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nIf $y =\\arcosh(x+1),$ then find $\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166593 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ce19d882-3c04-5ef1-8393-7de582df188d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166593 #edb/ref 1074 "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosine function is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\arcosh x) = \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{x^2-1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(x+1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(x+1)^{2}-1}}\\cdot (x+1)^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{({x}^{2}+2x+1)-1}}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+2x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x(x+2)}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166594 #edb/ref 1069 "e-8339" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166594 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nIf $y = \\artanh{4x},$ then find $\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166594 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d5eeb5a1-4bfd-5f1e-b261-548c91eec64b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166594 #edb/ref 1074 "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic tangent function is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\artanh x) = \\dfrac{1}{1-x^2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡4x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-{(4x)}^{2}}\\cdot {(4x)}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-16{x}^{2}}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{1-16{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166595 #edb/ref 1069 "e-8340" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166595 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nIf $w(x) = e^{2x}\\artanh{x},$ then $w'(x)=2e^{2x}\\artanh{x} + y(x).$ What is $y(x)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166595 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7cd3958b-aa1c-5c9a-b2ef-a21002aa7ff1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166595 #edb/ref 1074 "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nHere, we have the product of two functions $u(x) = e^{2x}$ and $v(x)=\\artanh{x}.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{w}^{′}(x) & ={({e}^{2x})}^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{artanh}⁡x+{e}^{2x}\\cdot {(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x)}^{′} \\\\  & =2{e}^{2x}\\cdot \\operatorname{artanh}⁡x+{e}^{2x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =2{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x+{{\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{1-{x}^{2}}}_{⏟}}_{y(x)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y(x) = \\dfrac{e^{2x}}{1 - x^2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166754 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186051084 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166754 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186167333 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166754 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186167354 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166754 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186516766 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166754 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186516789 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166754 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186516831 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166754 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186516832 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166754 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186516853 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166754 #edb/ref 1039 "Differentiating an Inverse Sinh Function" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166754 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186166592 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166754 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "8e25ae0e-d10c-5fa4-924e-4c6a7efebac6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166755 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186167334 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166755 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186167377 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166755 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186516779 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166755 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186516782 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166755 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186516858 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166755 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186516866 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166755 #edb/ref 1039 "Differentiating an Inverse Cosh Function" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166755 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186166593 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166755 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "eaab6e41-d34d-5eca-a41f-5ebe58a6b178" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166756 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 1