86516675 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516766 #edb/ref 1069 "q-341798" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516766 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516766 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nIf $y=5\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(3x),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516766 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "02e5e578-2923-57b2-a053-9b7f26dd5f2f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516766 #edb/ref 1074 "$$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic sine function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(3x)) \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(3x)) \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(3x)^{2}+1}}\\cdot (3x)^{′} \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{9{x}^{2}+1}}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{\\sqrt{9{x}^{2}+1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516767 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186516666 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516767 #edb/ref 1069 "q-337914" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516767 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516767 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nIf $y=2\\,\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(2x-1),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516767 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "032db788-5417-5a60-9bc5-91af6b1ca366" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516767 #edb/ref 1074 "$$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic tangent function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(2x-1)) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(2x-1)) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{1-{(2x-1)}^{2}}\\cdot {(2x-1)}^{′} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{1-(4{x}^{2}-4x+1)}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{4x-4{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{4x(1-x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x(1-x)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516779 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186516671 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516779 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95420" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516779 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516779 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nIf $y=3\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡{x}^{3},$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516779 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "18d061e8-8362-58bf-a0a8-8ae72383d1a4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516779 #edb/ref 1074 "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosine function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡{x}^{3}) \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡{x}^{3}) \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{({x}^{3})}^{2}-1}}\\cdot {({x}^{3})}^{′} \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{6}-1}}\\cdot 3{x}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{6}-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516782 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186516655 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516782 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95500" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516782 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516782 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nIf $y=2\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x),$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516782 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1e29259a-0f4e-5a3f-8104-feccbcb01883" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516782 #edb/ref 1074 "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosine function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)^{2}-1}}\\cdot (\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)^{′} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{ln}^{2}⁡x-1}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{x\\sqrt{{ln}^{2}⁡x-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516789 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186516752 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516789 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95419" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516789 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516789 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nIf $y=\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡2{x}^{2},$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516789 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2c958fbe-a6a3-5e35-b0a4-3549e7aa33c5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516789 #edb/ref 1074 "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic sine function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡2{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡2{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{(2{x}^{2})}^{2}+1}}\\cdot {(2{x}^{2})}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4{x}^{4}+1}}\\cdot 4x \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{4{x}^{4}+1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516800 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186516649 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516800 #edb/ref 1069 "q-344313" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516800 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516800 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nIf $y=4\\,\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(4x-1),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516800 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4b8c9d43-7595-500c-b3ee-cac3fe18402d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516800 #edb/ref 1074 "$$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic tangent function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(4x-1)) \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(4x-1)) \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{1-(4x-1)^{2}}\\cdot (4x-1)^{′} \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{1-(16{x}^{2}-8x+1)}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =16\\cdot \\frac{1}{8x-16{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =16\\cdot \\frac{1}{8x(1-2x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{x(1-2x)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516831 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186516686 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516831 #edb/ref 1069 "q-341812" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516831 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516831 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nIf $y=arsinh\\,(\\frac{x-3}{3}),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n| $\\text{d}y$ | $=$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{d}x$ |  | {{field-1}} |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516831 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a4eeca3f-6b34-52eb-84b0-9a3e73ae1349" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516831 #edb/ref 1074 "$$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic sine function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\,(arsinh\\,(\\frac{x-3}{3})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{(\\frac{x-3}{3})}^{2}+1}}\\cdot {(\\frac{x-3}{3})}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{9}+1}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{\\frac{(x-3)^{2}+9}{9}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(x-3)^{2}+9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{({x}^{2}-6x+9)+9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-6x+18}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516832 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186516693 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516832 #edb/ref 1069 "q-341820" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516832 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516832 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nIf $y=3\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{4}),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n| $\\text{d}y$ | $=$ | $24{x}^{3}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{d}x$ |  | {{field-1}} |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516832 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "aa4e4da2-fcbb-5aa7-a6f1-72dee8a3b1b4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516832 #edb/ref 1074 "$$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic sine function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{4})) \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{4})) \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{(\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{4})}^{2}+1}}\\cdot {(\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{4})}^{′} \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\frac{4}{9}{x}^{8}+1}}\\cdot \\frac{8}{3}{x}^{3} \\\\  & =8\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{3}}{\\sqrt{\\frac{4{x}^{8}+9}{9}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{24{x}^{3}}{\\sqrt{4{x}^{8}+9}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516844 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186516696 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516844 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95512" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516844 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516844 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nIf $y=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{6}}{3}),$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516844 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bc18352d-fce3-5063-b58a-47ac19e5cf8d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516844 #edb/ref 1074 "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic tangent function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{6}}{3})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{6}}{3})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{1-{(\\frac{{x}^{6}}{3})}^{2}}\\cdot {(\\frac{{x}^{6}}{3})}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{(1-\\frac{{x}^{12}}{9})}\\cdot 2{x}^{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{9{x}^{5}}{9-{x}^{12}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516853 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186516704 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516853 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95428" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516853 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516853 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nIf $y=6\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}),$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516853 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ca24054b-57db-5111-abb2-9a1c0e62e7da" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516853 #edb/ref 1074 "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic sine function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})) \\\\  & =6\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})) \\\\  & =6\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{(\\frac{x}{2})}^{2}+1}}\\cdot {(\\frac{x}{2})}^{′} \\\\  & =6\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+1}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516858 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186516733 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516858 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95504" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516858 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516858 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nIf $y=\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡2{x}^{2},$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516858 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d4997d00-7652-5cc7-a200-60025211209a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516858 #edb/ref 1074 "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosine function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡2{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡2{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{(2{x}^{2})}^{2}-1}}\\cdot {(2{x}^{2})}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4{x}^{4}-1}}\\cdot 4x \\\\  & =\\frac{6x}{\\sqrt{4{x}^{4}-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
